{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"agent_message","text":"Direct atomic aggregation is decisively slower (about 2.0 ms versus 0.38 ms for store plus reduction), so the route buffer stays. I found a more promising cache issue: the current grid schedules the same output column across 512 experts before moving to the next column, which evicts each expert’s routed activations. I’m transposing the launch order so all column tiles of one expert are adjacent and can reuse its 0.1–0.5 MiB activation tile through L2."}}
