{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The conditional half-tile kernel saves arithmetic but loses more matrix-core efficiency than it gains, so the proven 128-row kernel remains. I’m testing a low-risk concurrency improvement now: the shared gate/up projection is independent of route sorting and both routed GEMMs, so it can execute on a second stream and be joined before the fused final down/reduction."}}
